# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in this project is committed EXCEPT the raw AIS downloads in
# data/raw/, which GitHub cannot take: its hard limit is 100 MB per file and
# these run to 836 MB. They are unmodified public-domain US federal data from
# https://marinecadastre.gov/ais/ (date 2023-01-01). Re-download into data/raw/
# and run scripts/PIPELINE.py to regenerate everything downstream; the built
# datasets in data/ are committed, so no experiment here needs the raw file.
#
# Intermediates (data/windows_*.csv), superseded datasets (data/old8_*.csv),
# run logs and saved kernel matrices ARE committed: they are the record.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/

# Python environment -- regenerated from requirements.txt
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor/tool caches, not part of the research
.impeccable/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
